statements.statement:
The first mandatory result for \(\mathsf{QCan}\) is the following exhaustive alternative on \(G_{\mathrm{ABC}}\) and \(\mathcal J_{\mathrm{ABC}}\). Exactly one of the following holds: (i) \(\mathcal A_{G_{\mathrm{ABC}},\mathcal J_{\mathrm{ABC}}}^{\mathrm{raw}}=\mathcal A_{G_{\mathrm{ABC}},\mathcal J_{\mathrm{ABC}}}^{\mathrm{simp-q}}\), and there is a semialgebraic selector that, for every branch \(r\) and every \(
u\) in its quotient simplex, returns \(\lambda\in\Lambda_{G_{\mathrm{ABC}}}\) with \(\mathbb E_{
u}[\overline T_{G_{\mathrm{ABC}},\mathcal J_{\mathrm{ABC}}}]=\mathbb E_{\mu_{\lambda}}[T_{G_{\mathrm{ABC}},\mathcal J_{\mathrm{ABC}}}]\); or (ii) there exist a branch \(r\), an algebraic quotient mass \(
u\), and an algebraic vector \(x=\mathbb E_{
u}[\overline T_{G_{\mathrm{ABC}},\mathcal J_{\mathrm{ABC}}}]\in\mathcal A_{G_{\mathrm{ABC}},\mathcal J_{\mathrm{ABC}}}^{\mathrm{simp-q}}\setminus\mathcal A_{G_{\mathrm{ABC}},\mathcal J_{\mathrm{ABC}}}^{\mathrm{raw}}\), accompanied by an exact real-algebraic certificate of nonmembership. Alternative (ii) forces the endpoint compiler to retain the full raw-signature parameterization. After this test, can \(\mathsf{QCan}\) give, for every \(G\) and \(\mathcal J\), a necessary-and-sufficient latent-incidence criterion for \(\mathcal A_{G,\mathcal J}^{\mathrm{raw}}=\mathcal A_{G,\mathcal J}^{\mathrm{simp-q}}\), construct the selector when equality holds, and derive a nontrivial bound for \(|\overline\Omega_{G,\mathcal J}|\) in terms of \(N\), \(w_G\), and \(|\mathcal J|\)?
